{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["# Day 23 — Data pipelines: functions, generators, memory-efficient processing\n","Objectives:\n","- Build streaming pipelines with generators.\n","- Chunk large files.\n","- Compose transforms with .pipe."]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[],"source":["from pathlib import Path\n","def read_lines(path, chunk=1024):\n","    with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n","        while True:\n","            data = f.readlines(chunk)\n","            if not data: break\n","            for line in data: yield line.strip()\n","\n","# Example pipeline\n","def only_numbers(lines):\n","    for s in lines:\n","        if s.isdigit(): yield int(s)\n","\n","# list(only_numbers(read_lines('data.txt')))\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## Exercises\n","1) Build a CSV streaming cleaner (yield rows).\n","2) Compose generators to filter, map, and batch rows."]}]}
